  reading          applies to  a transfer of <amount> from Alice to Bob: every sender (Alice), every receiver (Bob), and every amount <amount> (a u64:
                               0 to 2^64 - 1); for every value of a (a u64: 0 to 2^64 - 1), b (a u64: 0 to 2^64 - 1)
                               every such call, accepted or rejected [default D2]
                   assuming    the balance of Alice is <a>; the balance of Bob is <b>; <amount> is at most the balance of Alice; the balance of Bob
                               plus <amount> is at most the largest balance a wallet can hold (2^64 - 1)
                   then        the call gives an answer [default D1]
                               the answer is Ok
                               the balance of Alice after the call, plus <amount>, equals the balance of Alice before it, exactly
                               the balance of Bob after the call equals the balance of Bob before it plus <amount>, exactly
                               the sum of the balances of every wallet named (Alice, Bob) after the call equals the sum of the balances of every wallet
                               named (Alice, Bob) before it
